#: processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn:104
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Editing a bean is not a separate ceremony: check off todo items as they happen, append measurements with the command and date that produced them, and record what you now know that the next agent does not. A bean whose body is a title is a placeholder, not a plan."
msgstr ""

#: processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn:94
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Idempotent. Claim BEFORE working, and note the branch, so a sibling session can see the item is taken rather than discovering it by collision."
msgstr ""

#: processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn:84
#. Diagram label
msgid "Leave it alone (coordinate instead)"
msgstr ""

#: processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn:157
#. Diagram label
msgid "mine / unclaimed"
msgstr ""

#: processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn:85
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Never resolve, scrap or delete a bean another session or a human owns. Claiming is how two sessions avoid picking the same item; closing someone else's is how one of them loses work it had not finished reporting."
msgstr ""

#: processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn:153
#. Diagram label
msgid "no"
msgstr ""

#: processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn:162
#. Diagram label
msgid "not wanted"
msgstr ""

#: processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn:91
#. Diagram label
msgid "Not yours to close"
msgstr ""

#: processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn:117
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Only once nothing is unchecked, and with a summary of what changed. The engine's `resolve` completes a bean only after the instance itself has completed — whether work is done is a judgement, and a bean is not closed on someone else's say-so."
msgstr ""

#: processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn:114
#. Diagram label
msgid "Outcome?"
msgstr ""

#: processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn:41
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Owns every transition on a bean it holds — check, create, claim, work, and the three-way outcome at the end — but GW_Owner is the one branch this lane cannot complete itself: the moment a bean turns out to be someone else's, the only correct move is to leave the whole lifecycle to Lane_Sibling rather than resolve, scrap or edit it from here."
msgstr ""

